-- title:
--   Supersingular valuation ring over k₀ with smooth-point packages
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a field $L$ the field `LaurentSeries L` is the field of formal Laurent series over $L$.
--
--   **Data.** A prime $q$ with $5 \le q$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Write $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$. Further: a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ (the subfield of `LaurentSeries κ` generated over $\kappa$ by `jqModC κ` and its $M'$-fold expansion `jqNModC κ M'`), with `hW` saying that $W$ consists exactly of the elements of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is, of the places $w$ which are rational (the structure map $\kappa \to \kappa(w)$ is surjective), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M' w`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen } κ\, M')$ lies in `ssJSet q κ`. A hypothesis `hle` that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (itself generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the expansions `qExpand ℚ d jq` for $d \mid M'$), is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the analogous base change of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ for $H = \ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times\bigr)$. A constant reduction datum $R_0$ of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, such that a constant lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ iff it lies in $A$ and then reduces compatibly, every non-zero element can be scaled by a constant into $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with non-zero residue, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with divisors of functions. The hypothesis `hR₀` pins $R_0$ down as coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally a distinguished element $s \in W$.
--
--   **The constants block $(k_0,\pi_0)$.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is a Henselian local ring (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); and `hκ`: every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$.
--
--   **The auxiliary prime block.** A prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **The layers block.** A type $\iota$, a family $K : \iota \to$ intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with each $K_n$ finite-dimensional over $k_0$, and valuation subrings $A_n \subseteq K_n$ with $x \in A_n \iff x \in A$ for all $x \in K_n$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Giving `fieldBar q M'` the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, there exist an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_0 \subseteq F_0$ such that the following hold.
--
--   (1) The join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   (2) For $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (4) The image of $\pi_0$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) There is $t \in W_0$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$: if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, then for every $n$ the image of the $n$-th coefficient of $p$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal.
--
--   (6) $W_0$ lies over $s$: for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, writing $\bar g$ for its coefficientwise image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, if $\bar g \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, if for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the inequality $\mathrm{ord}_P(\overline{\mathtt{jq}}) \ge 0$ forces $\mathrm{ord}_P(\bar g) \ge 0$, and if the $R_0$-residue of $\bar g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then the image of $\bar g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion given by `hle` lies in $F_0$, lies in $W_0$ there, and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $\bar g$, the difference of that image and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (7) Level-stability: for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}(q)$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` maps $F_0$ into $F_0$, and for $f \in F_0$ whose image also lies in $F_0$ one has $f \in W_0$ iff that image lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (8) For every field $F_{\mathrm{SS}}$ which is an algebra over $\kappa$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with values in $F_{\mathrm{SS}}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto $F_{\mathrm{SS}}$ with kernel the maximal ideal, constants belonging to $R.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when they lie in $A$ and reducing compatibly, and the scaling property), such that $R$ pins $W_0$, i.e. $f \in R.\mathrm{integers} \iff f \in W_0$ for all $f \in F_0$, both of the following hold.
--
--   (8a) *Drinfeld identification.* For every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ (here $\mathbb F_{q^2} =$ `GaloisField q 2`), assuming [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) — the quotient of $\kappa[x_0,x_1]$ by $(\mathtt{drinfeldPoly } q\,κ - 1)$ — is a domain, and for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}(q)$: there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ of $F_{\mathrm{SS}}$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ C_s`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the subfield of the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathtt{CoordRing } q\,κ)$ fixed by the subgroup generated by the images under `hFunctionFieldAction` of the pairs $(1,\zeta')$ with $\zeta' \in C_s$, such that $\#C_s = 2\cdot \mathtt{placeWidthChar } q\, M'\, s$ (namely `jWidthChar q` of the $j$-value of $s$ divided by $\mathtt{placeRamificationJ } M'\, s = \mathrm{ord}_s\bigl(\mathtt{jGeomGen} - s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen})\bigr)$), and such that $e$ is equivariant for the level automorphisms: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every witness that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and every witness that $(\mathtt{redQ } q\, \gamma, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(\gamma',u) \mapsto \det(\gamma')\,u^{q+1}$ on $GL_2(\mathbb Z/q) \times \mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$), and every $x \in F_{\mathrm{SS}}$, the image in the Drinfeld function field of $e$ applied to $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ of `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` at $x$ equals `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at $(\mathtt{redQ } q\,\gamma,1)$ applied to the image of $e(x)$.
--
--   (8b) *Smooth-point packages.* There exist a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{\mathrm{SS}}$ over $\kappa$, subrings $S_{Q,n} \subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'`, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_{Q,n} : A_n[X] \to S_{Q,n}$ and $\chi_{Q,n} : S_{Q,n} \to \kappa$, and sets $D_{Q,n}$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, indexed by places $Q$ of $F_{\mathrm{SS}}$ and by $n \in \iota$, such that $\#N = q+1$ and the following hold.
--
--   First, for every $Q \notin N$ and every $n$: the map $A_n \to \kappa$ sending $a$ to the residue of $a$ in $A$ is surjective; the image in `fieldBar q M'` of every $a \in A_n$ lies in $S_{Q,n}$; $\varphi_{Q,n}$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ for every $a \in A_n$; $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(X)) = 0$; for every $c \in A_n$ with residue $0$ in $\kappa$ there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi : S_{Q,n} \to A_n$ with $\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a)) = a$ for all $a \in A_n$, with the residue in $\kappa$ of $\chi(f)$ equal to $\chi_{Q,n}(f)$ for all $f$, and with $\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(X)) = c$; every $f \in S_{Q,n}$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue of the latter at $Q$ is the image of $\chi_{Q,n}(f)$ under $\kappa \to \kappa(Q)$; $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue has $\mathrm{ord}_Q$ equal to $1$; $D_{Q,n}$ consists exactly of the places $P$ that are rational, for which every $f \in S_{Q,n}$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for which the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ precisely when $\chi_{Q,n}(f) = 0$; for every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_{Q,n} \to A_n$ which is the identity on the $A_n$-coefficients and satisfies the residue compatibility above, there is exactly one place $P$ lying in $D_{Q,n}$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) = \chi(f)$ for all $f \in S_{Q,n}$; for every $P \in D_{Q,n}$ and every $f$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_n$, $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ iff $f h = g$ for some $g,h \in S_{Q,n}$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(h) \ne 0$; for every non-zero $f$ in that join with $\mathrm{ord}_P f = 0$ for all $P \in D_{Q,n}$ there are a non-zero $c \in K_n$ and a unit $u$ of $S_{Q,n}$ with $c \cdot f = u$ in `fieldBar q M'`; every $f$ in that join which lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and in the valuation subring of every $P \in D_{Q,n}$ lies in $S_{Q,n}$; and there is a finite subset $G \subseteq S_{Q,n}$ such that every $f \in S_{Q,n}$ satisfies $f h = g$ with $g,h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$ and with $h$ the image of a unit of $S_{Q,n}$.
--
--   Second, for every $Q \notin N$ the packages are compatible along the layers: $K_n \le K_{n'}$ implies $S_{Q,n} \le S_{Q,n'}$, and, for this inclusion, $K_n \le K_{n'}$ implies that $S_{Q,n'}$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_{Q,n}$ together with the image of $A_{n'}$; the elements $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ agree in `fieldBar q M'` for all $n, n'$; and $\chi_{Q,n'}$ restricted along the inclusion $S_{Q,n} \le S_{Q,n'}$ equals $\chi_{Q,n}$.
--
--   Third, the discs separate the ends: if $Q,Q' \notin N$ and some place $P$ lies both in $D_{Q,n}$ and in $D_{Q',n}$ for some $n$, then $Q = Q'$.
--
--   Fourth, for $Q \notin N$, every $n$ and every $P \in D_{Q,n}$, the order $\mathrm{ord}_P$ of the image in `fieldBar q M'` of `jq` is $\ge 0$.
--
--   Fifth, equivariance: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}(q)$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every witness that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every place $Q$ of $F_{\mathrm{SS}}$: the translate of $Q$ by the induced residual automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ lies in $N$ iff $Q$ does, and if $Q \notin N$ then for every $n$ one has $\{P : \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D_{Q,n}\} = D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\,\cdot\,Q, n}$.
--
--   This is the small-constants layer in the construction of the supersingular components of the stable model of $X_H(q^2M')$ at $q$: over an admissible field of constants $k_0$ it produces a residually transcendental discrete valuation ring $W_0$ lying over a prescribed supersingular place $s$ of the level-$M'$ curve, stable under the level automorphisms, identifies the associated reduced field with a quotient of the Drinfeld function field equivariantly for $\Gamma_0(M')$, and supplies, at each finite layer $K_n$ and each end $Q$ outside a set of $q+1$ ends, an étale chart with its residue discs. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts), which passes from $k_0$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
